  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Sofia University, established in 1975, is a private for-profit institution located in Palo Alto, California. Originally founded as the Institute of Transpersonal Psychology, it has evolved to offer a diverse range of programs in psychology, business, and computer science.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>Sofia University fosters an inclusive and engaging student life. The University provides you with mental health and wellness support through its counselling services.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>Sofia University does not provide on-campus housing. However, the University assists you in finding stay options through a list of agencies and websites.</p><p>Additionally, if you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, <a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\">download our app</a> and check out the Stays feature!</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Library</strong><br>Sofia University has a well-equipped library. It consists of about 17,000 books and an impressive collection of over 100,000 e-books. You can also access online scholarly materials through the library's portal.</p>",
      "image": null,
